Project 58, nklein-repair-fixture (inventory allocator variant). SECOND of the 3-defect chain.
Card 1 (already landed on your branch) made src/stock-ledger.mjs's applyMovements pure -- it now returns a new
snapshot instead of mutating. That unmasks a second, pre-existing bug in src/allocator.mjs that this card fixes.

## The defect (stale-read, src/allocator.mjs)
`allocate()` calls `applyMovements(snapshot, [...])` inside its loop but throws away the return value and keeps
using the stale `snapshot` binding. Before card 1, this was invisible because applyMovements mutated the object
in place, so the stale binding happened to already reflect the change. Now that applyMovements returns a fresh
object every time, `allocate()`'s per-line `free` calculation never sees any line's own effect on stock, so two
lines for the same sku can together take more than the shelf holds, and the returned snapshot no longer reflects
any allocation at all.

## The fix -- replace src/allocator.mjs verbatim with:
```js
import { reservedFor } from "./reservations.mjs";
import { applyMovements, unitsOf } from "./stock-ledger.mjs";

/**
 * Allocate an order against a stock snapshot, line by line in order.
 *
 * A line may take at most what is free for its sku — units on hand, minus units held by live reservations, minus
 * whatever earlier lines of this same order already took. Two lines for one sku can therefore never add up to more
 * than the shelf holds.
 *
 * Returns `{ allocations, snapshot }` where `snapshot` is the stock that results. The caller's snapshot is a value
 * and is left exactly as it was, so the same allocation can be replayed from it and give the same answer.
 */
export function allocate(snapshot, reservations, order) {
	const allocations = [];
	let current = snapshot;
	for (const line of order.lines) {
		const free = unitsOf(current, line.sku) - reservedFor(reservations, line.sku);
		const take = Math.max(0, Math.min(line.quantity, free));
		allocations.push({ sku: line.sku, quantity: take });
		current = applyMovements(current, [{ sku: line.sku, delta: -take }]);
	}
	return { allocations, snapshot: current };
}

/** Total units allocated for a sku across an allocation result. */
export function allocatedFor(allocations, sku) {
	return allocations
		.filter((allocation) => allocation.sku === sku)
		.reduce((total, allocation) => total + allocation.quantity, 0);
}
```
Exported names unchanged (`allocate`, `allocatedFor`). This is the only file this card edits in src/.

